  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 21, 2026, a significant earthquake with a magnitude of 7.2 was recorded in the Maluku Barat Daya region of Indonesia. The Badan Meteorologi, Klimatologi, dan Geofisika (BMKG) monitored the seismic activity and issued an official assessment confirming that the event did not pose a tsunami threat to the surrounding coastal areas. Further technical analysis by officials identified the source of the earthquake as originating from the Benioff zone, a region of subduction where tectonic plates interact. This event has been tracked by multiple news outlets reporting on the incident as it unfolded. The incident remains a focal point for regional seismic monitoring efforts, distinct from other reported seismic activities occurring in separate geographical locations during the same timeframe.",
